WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:04.737
 Without further
ado, here we go.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.739
 Cool, man.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:10.343
 [grunting]

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.112
 It will.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.816
 John, my congratulations.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.551
You've landed yourselves
in the final round

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.619
of this competition.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.120
Now we're sending you
back to your home forages

00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:23.323
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:29.762
That weapon is the Greek kopis.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.131
Bladesmiths, you'll have five
days at your home forages

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.432
in which to complete
this challenge.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:34.934
At the end of those
five days, you'll

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:38.805
return and present your kopises
to our panel of expert judges.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.207
And after they thoroughly
tested the hell out of them,

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.775
they'll declare one
of you the Forged

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:46.745
in Fire champion who leaves
here with a check for $10,000.

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:47.713
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.847
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:49.581
 Good luck.

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:52.385 line:7%
 Good luck.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:55.187
 Feels great to be
back in my home forge.

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:56.522
I'm excited to get started.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:01:00.093
I'm going to do a wrap or
a sand mod construction.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.361
My damascus is on the outside.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.497
There's a solid
layer of 15 and 20.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:09.368
And then down the center
is one solid piece of 5160.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:12.472
It should be really
pretty and tough.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.677
 I'm back at the home forge,
I'm getting ready to go.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.946
And this entire piece
is going to be made out

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:24.984
of Damascus with an integral
guard and an integral pommel

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.018
built into it.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:29.188
So without further
ado, here we go.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:32.858
If I at the end of day have
a rough shape of a sword,

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:34.060
I'll be really happy.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.828
It's 30 layers right now.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:39.298
I'm going to cut it into
sections, probably three,

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:42.402
to have a layer count about 90.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:45.872 line:7%
OK, we have a long way to go.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.173 line:7%
 It's day two.

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:50.443
I have to make some fullering
dyes for this blade.

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:53.646
This is the bottom section
of a railroad track.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.248
I have to just round
the top off to get

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:57.717
the right shape that I want.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.892
The fuller lines are
really clean, symmetrical.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:08.828
It's exactly what
I was hoping for.

00:02:08.894 --> 00:02:10.830
 It's the start of day three.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:14.233
We're going to work on
the guard and the pommel.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.468
Got a lot of work to do.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.337
It's going to be a
lot of detailed work.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.205
It's going to be slow.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:22.008
I feel like a dentist.

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.877
And then I've got
to quench the blade.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.981
Everything that I've done
since I've picked up a hammer

00:02:29.047 --> 00:02:31.284
is coming down to this point.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.655
I hope that this works out.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:38.524
It's perfectly straight.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.226
[clapping]

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:43.762 line:7%
I got a straight blade!

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:44.830
 It's day 4.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.065
I'm excited.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:50.136
I think, basically, I just have
to finish up my handle today.

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:52.338
I'm going to pin these
two pieces of brass

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:55.841
to either side of the blade
to hold them in place while I

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.409
silver solder.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.012 line:0%
Going to heat up
the guard a little,

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:05.385 line:0%
let the heat travel up the blade
and up towards that solder.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.520
Think this sword is
going to look awesome.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:10.656
The color combination with
the brass and the dark

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:13.626
handle scales, it's just
all coming together.

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:15.394
I'm really stoked.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.497
I still have one more
piece to meet parameters.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.300
I need to connect my
pommel to the guard.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.669
This is going to go
through the horse's mouth,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:27.272
and it's going to
bend in a V, and come

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:29.342
down here into the guard.

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:31.110
I want to make it
look like rain's

00:03:31.176 --> 00:03:34.213
coming from the horse's mouth.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.882
I like it.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.916 line:7%
That's good.

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:38.984 line:7%
 This is the last day.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.953
I've got to put scales on.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:45.157
When your band saw breaks,
you've got to improvise.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:49.462
I have never put scales
on a blade that's got

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:52.298
an integral pommel and guard.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.134
I just may have made a
really, really big mistake.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:58.204
My pin doesn't fit right.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.739
I drilled the wrong hole.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:00.773
I'm in a panic mode.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.344
So on day five, I've got
to make the new handle.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.911
It's coming along.

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:07.446
Now I'm feeling pretty good.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:11.250
Making this kopis was a
really, really tall order.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:14.587
I feel like I've done my
best work that I've ever

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.991
done as a bladesmith right now.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:22.361
It will cut.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.829
 All right,
bladesmiths, to find out

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.365
what kind of lethal damage
your weapon will do,

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.301
I will take your kopis
and deliver some killing

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:31.070
blows to this ballistics dummy.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.571
John, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:33.205
 Ready.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:34.573
I'm pretty nervous.

00:04:34.606 --> 00:04:37.676
There's no way to prepare
yourself for this moment.

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:40.680
I'm just going to hope
that my blade survives.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:47.820
[grunting]

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:08.941
 Cool, man.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:10.643
 All right, John, let's
talk about your kopis here.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.478
There was a little
crack that goes

00:05:12.544 --> 00:05:15.748
around the edge on both sides.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.150
When I saw the tip, I thought
it was going be tip heavy.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.118
It's not.

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.186
There's good recovery with this.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.688
It's a very powerful
weapon, sir.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.256
It will kill.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:25.358
 Thank you.

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:26.525
 All right, Mike.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:27.393
It's time to have
fun with your blade.

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:28.127
Are you ready?

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.929
 I'm ready.

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:35.535
 [grunting]

00:05:53.885 --> 00:05:54.920
 Good job.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:55.855
 Thanks.

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:56.889
 All right, Mike.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.657
Let's talk about your
Greek kopis right here.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:02.295
It is heavier, but every
shot that I go in there cuts.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:03.529
You have a sharp edge.

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:07.032
But more importantly,
sir, it will kill.

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:07.833
 Thank you.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:08.634
 Good job.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.873
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:15.475
Now, to test the
strength, durability,

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.976
and overall construction
of your Greek

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.879
kopises I'll be attacking
these two soldiers.

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:20.646
John, you're up.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.213
You ready?

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.016
 Ready.

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:27.987
[clanging]

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:36.728
 All right, John, first off,
that small crack we noticed

00:06:36.795 --> 00:06:40.799
has not opened up at
all, which is great.

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:43.302
Your blade took some
minor deformation.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:44.670
A little bit of roll.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.373
But overall, it's
a strong blade.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.140
Well done.

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:49.174
 Thank you.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.275
 All right, Mike.
You're up.

00:06:50.342 --> 00:06:51.077
You ready?

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.412
 I'm ready.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:56.549
[clanging]

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:08.727
 All right, so Mike, your edge
took a little bit of damage

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:09.962
here.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:13.499
And then up here, it just sort
of peeled a hair off your edge.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.001
But other than
that, this blade is

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:18.471
still sharp all the way down.

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:21.040
It's got some heft to it,
but your handle construction

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:21.907
does make up for it.

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.876
But most of all,
it's a strong blade.

00:07:23.942 --> 00:07:24.510
Nicely done, Mike.

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:25.511
 Thank you.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:29.581
 All right, bladesmiths,
to test the edge

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:32.184
of your Greek kopis, I
will take your weapon,

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:34.653
and I will slice
across these rugs.

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:36.254
John, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:36.321 --> 00:07:37.056
 Ready.

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:43.395
[thudding]

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:44.997
[crash]

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:01.113
 All right, John.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.515
The edge here is sharp.

00:08:02.581 --> 00:08:04.350
On this last one, not so much.

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:07.786
But as we can see on the
other rugs, it will cut.

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:09.155
- Thank you.
- All right, Mike.

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:09.955
It's your turn.

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:10.522
You ready?

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:13.258
 I'm ready.

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:16.229
[slicing]

00:08:27.672 --> 00:08:29.575
 All right, Mike, first
up, the forward weight

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:32.078
that you have on your
blade here lends itself

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:34.547
to do a beautiful vertical cut.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.082
But on a diagonal cut,
because of the forward weight

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:39.785
being there, it feels more
like a chopper than a slasher.

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:44.456
So it cut in, but it didn't
slice in to control that.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:47.859
It's a sharp edge,
and it will cut.

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:48.894
 Thank you.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:51.129
 John, Mike, both of
you made high-performance

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:54.700
blades that did very well
in our weapons tests.

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:57.003
Our next Forged in
Fire champion is--

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:01.207
John.

00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:02.341
Congratulations.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:03.876
You're the new Forged
in Fire champion.

00:09:03.909 --> 00:09:05.311
Mike, I want you to
know that the judges

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:08.014
and I are proud as hell of
what you've turned in, man.

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:10.615
It was a competitive blade,
and it really did come

00:09:10.682 --> 00:09:13.719
down to the finest details.

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:17.389
But I have to ask you to
please surrender your kopis.

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:21.760
 It really makes me feel good
that the judging was so close.

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:25.031
This competition was
really tough for me.

00:09:25.064 --> 00:09:29.734
It tested a lot of new skills
that I hadn't done before.

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:31.169
It was a big win for myself.

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:34.406
It was a great competition
and a great experience,

00:09:34.472 --> 00:09:38.010
and I'd do it all over again.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:39.044
 John, congratulations.

00:09:39.077 --> 00:09:40.780
You're our new Forged
in Fire champion,

00:09:40.813 --> 00:09:43.014
and that's the title that
comes with a check for $10,000.

00:09:43.081 --> 00:09:46.519
Please present your
blade to the judges.

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:48.921
 I'm unbelievably happy.

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:51.389
I'm a new bladesmith,
and it's something that I

00:09:51.423 --> 00:09:53.625
want to do in the future.

00:09:53.692 --> 00:09:56.762
To walk into this
world of bladesmithing

00:09:56.795 --> 00:10:00.599
and then join "Forged in
Fire," and compete and win it,

00:10:00.665 --> 00:10:03.803
it doesn't get any
better than that.

